tags: any, text

A format of an environment variable: any value. The caller gives any bytes with no NUL
byte. A node and a caller check no other thing: not UTF-8, not a length.

Example: the value 8080, or a JSON text.

A node gives the variable to the process of the service only if its name is a C
identifier. A node refuses a value with a NUL byte.

=== formal
class=format
name=any
value=any bytes with no byte of the value 0; no other check
